  "result": "I graded Riley's submission s2 for quiz 0001 and wrote `grades/0001-s2.json`. They got 3 items correct, 2 partial and 1 wrong.\n\n| Item | Verdict | Feedback |\n|---|---|---|\n| q1 | correct | The loop is what makes a system an agent. |\n| q2 | correct | The model only writes a request that names the tool and its arguments. |\n| q3 | wrong (M6) | They chose \"it will eventually fix it\", but a stuck loop needs a stopping condition such as a step limit. |\n| q4 | partial (M4) | The answer 4 is right, but their reason says the model runs the tools itself. The program runs them. |\n| q5 | correct | They gave both what happens and why. |\n| q6 | partial | The model uses each tool's full description and parameters, not just its name. |\n\n**Summary:** Riley has the loop down. Two ideas need work. The program runs the tools, not the model (q4). A loop needs a stopping condition, and the model picks tools from their descriptions (q3, q6).\n\n**Next step:** Take `check_calendar` and write its name, a one-sentence description and its parameters. Then note who runs it and what ends the loop. After that we can move on to context and memory.\n\nI also added `learning-records/0003-quiz-1-retake-program-runs-tools.md` and updated the quiz 0001 note in `NOTES.md`. `submissions/s1.json` is still ungraded.",
